{{Otheruses|def=no|the [[free-to-play]] variant of this guide|Optimal quest guide/Free-to-play/Ironman}}

This guide is intended for [[Ironman Mode|iron accounts]]. For the regular guide, see [[Optimal quest guide|here]].

==Guide==

This guide is designed to provide you with a path to complete all quests while avoiding early or long skilling grinds. It will include some notes for efficiency where it will save you time later to do certain actions during quests. For example, completing Diary tasks, gathering items, and completing other quest steps while in the area. Following the guide fairly closely until the completion of [[Holy Grail]] is recommended, as the early path is quite optimised for completing quests together in the early areas, skipping early combat training and unlocking some useful transportation options to make future activities easier.

This guide puts most lamp rewards on [[Herblore]] whenever possible, as this is generally the slowest skill to train as an ironman due to difficulty obtaining the ingredients. Any [[experience lamp]]s or [[book of knowledge|books of knowledge]] received through [[random events]] may also be used on {{SCP|Herblore|link=yes}}. The questing order assumes that you have followed the advice on experience rewards exactly for the sake of unlocking the next quests in the list. You may need to do additional training or skip certain quests if choosing another skill to lamp.

While following this guide, also consider what other activities you might want to do alongside it depending on your goals. Skills like {{SCP|Farming|link=yes}} and {{SCP|Hunter|link=yes}} in particular are usually trained at set timings alongside other activities, and as such may be trained to a higher level earlier than the guide suggests. {{SCP|Prayer|link=yes}} will make certain quests easier if trained earlier for protection prayers, and {{SCP|Herblore|link=yes}} gives you access to potions. {{SCP|Agility|link=yes}} gives you the largest benefits at early levels due to run regeneration. For most skills however, skipping early levels through quests will be faster than early skill grinds, as you won't have access to the fastest skilling methods. When {{SCP|Slayer|link=yes}} is trained on the side, it is recommended to use [[Konar quo Maten|Konar]] as soon as possible, due to the possibility to loot [[Magic logs]] from the [[Brimstone chest]], these are required for [[Desert Treasure I]].

When doing skilling grinds outside of this guide, keep in mind what quests you may be able to complete earlier for useful unlocks. For example, training 49 {{SCP|Firemaking|link=yes}} earlier will allow you to complete [[Tears of Guthix]] earlier, which provides the player with a short minigame that will reward experience points in their lowest skill once a week. You may also prioritise quests that give experience in the skill you are planning to grind, which will allow you to skip slow early levels. For a useful list of quest experience rewards see [[Quest experience rewards|here]].

Gaining access to transportation methods will allow you to complete many quests faster. This guide prioritises unlocking the [[Ardougne Cloak 1]], [[spirit trees]], [[fairy rings]] and [[gnome gliders]] early as these provide you with free teleports to multiple useful locations. It is also useful to gain access to transportation methods outside of completing quests, such as [[minigame teleports]]. New players on a budget may use [[games necklace(8)]] to teleport around or for access to a bank.

The [[Ironman guide]] is a good place to find general tips for activities, money making, and unlocks to prioritise.

